> Is there something in the code that actually makes displacement really
> more powerful than invisibility? 

Yes.

The effect of invisibility, roughly, is to cause a monster to think that 
you are within 1 square of your actual position.

The effect of displacement, roughly, is to cause a monster to think that 
you are within 2 squares of your actual position.

So monsters are *much* more likely to wander off in the wrong direction 
with displacement than invisibility.  With displacement, a monster right 
next to you might walk directly away.  Won't happen with invisibility.

Furthermore, the effect of displacement + invisibility is identical to 
the (weaker) effect of just invisibility with most monsters.

